      "page_title": "One Thread, Six Phases",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. One Thread Only",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Node runs your JS on ONE thread, one call stack.",
            "Every synchronous line blocks every other request.",
            "A 2s `for` loop = 2s of dead server, for everyone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Blocking vs Non-Blocking",
          "items": [
            "Blocking: returns only when work is done.",
            "`fs.readFileSync(p)` — the stack waits.",
            "Non-blocking: returns now, result delivered later.",
            "`fs.readFile(p, cb)` — the loop keeps going."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. I/O-Bound vs CPU-Bound",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Async fixes WAITING on I/O, not CPU work.",
            "Hashing, parsing, image resize stay blocking.",
            "Concurrency = interleaved in-flight ops, one thread.",
            "Parallelism needs `worker_threads` / `child_process`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "app.get('/hash', (req, res) => {",
            "  res.end(bcrypt.hashSync(pw, 12)); // serial!",
            "});",
            "// bcrypt.hash(pw, 12) -> threadpool, concurrent"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Runtime Is Not Single-Threaded",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Work",
            "Handled by",
            "Pool slot?"
          ],
          "rows": [
