          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Loop Phases In Order",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "timers",
              "pending cbs",
              "idle/prepare",
              "poll",
              "check",
              "close"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Runs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "timers",
              "setTimeout / setInterval"
            ],
            [
              "poll",
              "I/O cbs; blocks here when idle"
            ],
            [
              "check",
              "setImmediate — always after poll"
            ],
            [
              "close",
              "socket.on('close')"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Timers are a floor, never a guarantee.",
            "Microtasks drain BETWEEN every macrotask callback.",
            "Order: `process.nextTick` queue, then promises.",
            "Recursive nextTick starves the loop; setImmediate can't."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Memorise this puzzle",
          "text": "At top level, `setTimeout(fn,0)` vs `setImmediate` is NON-deterministic (depends on loop startup). Inside an I/O callback, `setImmediate` always wins."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Trace The Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "log('1'); log('2');",
            "process.nextTick(() => log('nextTick'));",
            "Promise.resolve().then(() => log('promise'));",
            "setTimeout(() => log('timeout'), 0);",
            "setImmediate(() => log('immediate'));"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prints: 1 2 nextTick promise timeout immediate.",
            "Sync code first — it owns the stack until it returns.",
            "Each phase drains up to a system max, then moves on.",
            "So one phase cannot indefinitely starve the next."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Loop Lag",
          "items": [
            "Lag = should-have-fired minus did-fire.",
            "`perf_hooks.monitorEventLoopDelay()`.",
            "Browsers have no nextTick — demos don't port 1:1."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Error-First Contract",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "fs.readFile('a.txt','utf8', (err, data) => {",
            "  if (err) return cb(err);   // return!",
            "  cb(null, data.trim());     // null on success",
            "});"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
