    {
      "page_title": "Ordering & The Error-First Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Error is ALWAYS the first parameter, `null` on success.",
            "Miss the `return` and the callback fires twice.",
            "The runtime invokes your callback, not your code.",
            "So `try/catch` around the call cannot catch inside it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Throw = death",
          "text": "A throw inside a callback with no handler becomes an `uncaughtException` and kills the process."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Zalgo & Once",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// never sometimes-sync, sometimes-async",
            "if (hit) return process.nextTick(",
            "  () => cb(null, hit));   // defer the cache path",
            "fs.readFile(k, cb);"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Call the callback exactly once — no more, no less.",
            "Guard with `let called = false` or `once()`.",
            "Matters most when wrapping event-based APIs."
          ]
        },
        {
