        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Fan Out, Then Partition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const rs = await Promise.allSettled(jobs);",
            "const ok = rs.filter(r => r.value !== undefined);",
            "const bad = rs.filter(r => r.reason);  // retry"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parallel START creates concurrency, not `await`.",
            "`await Promise.all([getA(), getB()])` — calls made first.",
            "Any iterable works; non-promises get `Promise.resolve`d.",
            "10,000 items = 10,000 sockets. Combinators have NO limit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. async Returns A Promise",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`return 1` fulfills with 1; `throw e` rejects with e.",
            "`await p` suspends the function, resumes in a microtask.",
            "It never blocks the loop or the thread.",
            "`await 1` still costs one microtask tick — not free."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "async function f() {",
            "  const a = await g();",
            "  return a + 1;",
            "}",
            "// desugars to: g().then(a => a + 1)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. try/catch Comes Back",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "try { await q(sql); }",
            "catch (e) { log(e); }",
            "finally { client.release(); }  // always"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Intermediate values become plain `const`s — no pyramid.",
            "That readability win is the whole point of the syntax.",
            "Top-level `await`: ESM only (.mjs / type: module).",
            "CommonJS still needs an async IIFE."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Iteration Rules",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`forEach(async …)` is fire-and-forget — return ignored.",
            "Use `for...of` (serial) or `map` + `Promise.all`.",
            "`for await (const c of stream)` walks async iterables.",
            "Idiomatic for streams and paginated APIs."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "async function* pages(url) {",
            "  let next = url;",
            "  while (next) { const p = await get(next);",
            "    yield p.items; next = p.next; }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
