      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Why Bound It",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unbounded fan-out: EMFILE, ECONNRESET, 429s, OOM.",
            "It drains DB pools and blows memory too.",
            "Little's Law: in-flight ≈ arrival rate × latency.",
            "The limit is the knob that caps in-flight work."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const limit = pLimit(5);",
            "await Promise.all(items.map(",
            "  i => limit(() => fetchOne(i))   // THUNK",
            "));"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The one-character bug",
          "text": "`limit(fetchOne(i))` is wrong — the call already started, so the limiter gates nothing. The function must be deferred."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Roll Your Own Pool",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "let i = 0;",
            "const worker = async () => {",
            "  while (i < n) await task(list[i++]);  // cursor",
            "};",
            "await Promise.all([1,2,3,4,5].map(worker));"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Semaphore: a counter plus a queue of resolvers.",
            "`acquire()` returns a promise when a slot is free.",
            "`release()` pops the queue and resolves the next waiter."
          ]
        },
